---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title="Cookies on NZSalary.com: What Is Set in Your Browser" description="Cookies and local storage on NZSalary.com: none for the calculators, Microsoft Clarity for audience measurement with no consent banner, and how to block it in your browser." lang={lang} noindex={true} jsonLd={[breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: route('home', lang) }, { name: 'Cookies', path: route('cookies', lang) }])]} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Cookies' }]}>
  <header class="mb-6"><h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-navy-900 md:text-4xl">Cookies</h1></header>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <p>The calculators do not use cookies. They keep your inputs only in the page itself, and in the address bar when you use the share link.</p>
    <p>We measure how the site is used with Microsoft Clarity: clicks, scrolling, pages viewed and their address, replayed as anonymous sessions and heatmaps. What you type into a field is masked in your browser before anything is sent. Clarity sets the cookies <code>_clck</code> (one year) and <code>_clsk</code> (one day), and Microsoft may set <code>MUID</code> and <code>CLID</code> on its own domains. No advertising cookie is set.</p>
    <p>Clarity loads when the page opens: the site shows no notice and no consent banner. To refuse it, block third-party cookies or the domain <code>clarity.ms</code> in your browser, and clear site data to remove cookies already set. The calculators work without them.</p>
    <p>Questions: see the <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a>.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
